218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The biggest weakness appears to be a conversion problem rather than an absence of aspiration. Students move through school and university with some exposure to entrepreneurship, but that exposure too rarely translates into extracurricular participation, venture formation or sustained entrepreneurial activity.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (The practical implication is that universities should move beyond awareness-raising alone. The strategic need is for more experiential, discipline-integrated entrepreneurship education, stronger venture validation pathways, better access to advice, and more visible routes from study to entrepreneurial action.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
